{%- comment -%}
  Inline wordmark lockup — the emblem stands in for the first repeated letter,
  so the brand reads GL[mark]RIOUS on one line. Used in the nav bar, the nav
  pill and the menu overlay header.

  The theme's own emblem is inline SVG on `currentColor`, so it takes the
  colour of the surface it sits on. It used to be two PNG cuts, light and
  dark, chosen by an `on_dark` flag — which is what `currentColor` does by
  itself, and correctly for any colour scheme rather than only for black and
  white. `on_dark` is therefore accepted and ignored, so existing callers do
  not need touching.

  Accepts:
    source  - the Huge Text value.
    size    - 'sm' (nav), 'md' (default), 'lg' (menu overlay).
    on_dark - accepted for compatibility; the emblem follows currentColor.
{%- endcomment -%}

{%- liquid
  assign source = source | strip | upcase
  assign letters = source | split: ''
  assign scale = size | default: 'md'

  comment
    Find the first letter that has already appeared — the emblem replaces it.
  endcomment
  assign mark_index = -1
  assign seen = ''
  for letter in letters
    if seen contains letter
      assign mark_index = forloop.index0
      break
    endif
    assign seen = seen | append: letter
  endfor
-%}

<span class="lockup lockup--{{ scale }}" role="img" aria-label="{{ source }}">
  {%- for letter in letters -%}
    {%- if forloop.index0 == mark_index -%}
      {%- render 'wordmark-mark' -%}
    {%- else -%}
      {%- liquid
        assign is_lead = false
        if mark_index > 0 and forloop.index0 < mark_index
          assign is_lead = true
        endif
      -%}
      <span class="lockup__letter{% if is_lead %} lockup__letter--lead{% endif %}" aria-hidden="true">{{ letter }}</span>
    {%- endif -%}
  {%- endfor -%}
</span>
